--- body ---
## Context

The pre-commit hook template git-erg installs (and re-emits on every
`erg install --hooks`) tells a user whose `tickets/erg` is missing to:

    ERROR: tickets/erg not found. Run 'make build' first.

That remediation is wrong for any project that **vendors** the committed
binary at `tickets/erg` rather than building it — e.g. the Imperial Dragon
Harness, where there is no `make build` target; the binary is refreshed via
`git pull` or rebuilt from this (git-erg) source. Because the string lives in
the template embedded in the binary, an adopter cannot durably hand-edit it:
the next `erg install --hooks` re-emits the managed block and clobbers the
fix. So the durable fix belongs here, upstream.

Filed from IDH tracker tickets/0231 (cross-repo). Only the `Run 'make build'
first` remediation is wrong — the twin "do not commit tickets/erg in feature
branches" line is correct (the binary is committed on main only); leave it.

## Relevant files

- `src/go/install.go:107` — the authoritative embedded hook template string
  (`echo "ERROR: tickets/erg not found. Run 'make build' first." >&2`). This
  is what gets compiled into the binary and re-emitted by `erg install --hooks`.
- `src/go/assets/integration.md:59` — the documentation mirror of the same line.
- `src/go/version.go:180` — `{"./build/erg", "run: make build"}` is a
  build-provenance label, NOT hook text; do not touch (verify in review).

## Actions

1. Replace the remediation wording in `src/go/install.go` with text that is
   true both for git-erg itself (which has `make build`) and for vendored-binary
   adopters, e.g.:
       ERROR: tickets/erg not found. Build it from the git-erg source
       (make build there), or 'git pull' if your project vendors the
       committed binary.
2. Update the `src/go/assets/integration.md` mirror to match.
3. Rebuild the binary so the embedded template carries the new text.

## Test

- A ratchet/unit test asserting the freshly built binary's hook template no
  longer contains `Run 'make build' first`:
      strings ./build/erg | grep -q "Run 'make build' first"   # must be empty
  Prove RED against the current binary first.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `src/go/install.go` hook template uses agnostic remediation wording.
- [ ] `src/go/assets/integration.md` mirror updated to match.
- [ ] Ratchet test: built binary contains no `Run 'make build' first`.
- [ ] `make check` (or git-erg's equivalent) passes.

## Cross-repo note

IDH tracker tickets/0231 stays open until this lands AND IDH re-vendors the
corrected binary. After this merges + the binary is rebuilt/released, IDH
picks it up on a main-only merge and closes 0231 there.
